{
  "comment": "Key combinations in the kit's one notation: the cases kit/src/Interop/ShortcutCombo.cs (ShortcutComboTests) and kit/web/kit.js's kit.shortcuts (web/tests/shortcuts.test.mjs) both pass, so the server's check of an admin's setting and the browser's check of a user's override agree. 'normalize': what someone typed -> the canonical combination ('' for nothing, null for text that isn't one). 'fromJellyfinEnhanced': a key as Jellyfin Enhanced's settings hold it -> the combination the 12.8 to 12.11 listener compares it with (null when no key press can equal it); C# only. 'fromJellyfinEnhanced1212': the same key -> the key presses JE 12.12's listener acts on, in the kit's notation (it reads b as B and modifiers in any order, drops a Shift+ before a shifted symbol, and takes a one-character key other than a letter or the space bar with or without Shift; [] when no key press can equal it); C# only. 'events': a keydown event -> its combination in the kit's notation, as Jellyfin Enhanced 12.8 to 12.11 build it; JavaScript only. 'pressable': whether a keyboard can send the combination's key.",
